            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-112321-libgssapi-krb5-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-112321 high vulnerability for libgssapi-krb5-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The AUTH_GSSAPI handler in lib/rpc/svc_auth_gssapi.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) does not free decoded arguments on certain error paths, which allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (memory exhaustion in kadmind) via crafted AUTH_GSSAPI_INIT requests that trigger authentication failures."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112321",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-112321\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libgssapi-krb5-2\nVersion: 1.22.1-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-112321](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112321)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-112321**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | libgssapi-krb5-2  | 1.22.1-3  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-112321](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112321)  |\n"
