            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-86412-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-86412 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A remote HTTP server can set a cookie that curl accepts and writes to a Netscape cookie jar but cannot reload. On the next invocation using the same path for `--cookie` and `--cookie-jar`, curl fails before connecting, then the cleanup procedure replaces the jar with an empty file, deleting cookies for unrelated domains."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86412",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-86412\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-86412](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86412)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-86412**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-86412](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-86412)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/curl@8.22.0-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "8.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92386-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92386 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "When writing a long cookie name and value to a Netscape cookie jar, a remote HTTP server can make `curl` write a record that exceeds its line-length parsing limit. Consequently, any subsequent `curl` invocation reading from that same cookie jar using `--cookie` silently aborts parsing prematurely upon encountering the too long line, ignoring all subsequent valid cookies in the file."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92386",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92386\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-92386](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92386)",
