            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-112323-libgssapi-krb5-2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-112323 high vulnerability for libgssapi-krb5-2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "The AUTH_GSSAPI handler in lib/rpc/svc_auth_gssapi.c in MIT Kerberos 5 (aka krb5) 1.5.2 and later allows remote attackers to cause a denial of service (memory exhaustion in kadmind) by sending repeated failed AUTH_GSSAPI_INIT requests. Each failed request allocates client state that is only freed after a 15-minute expiration timeout, allowing an attacker to accumulate memory faster than it is reclaimed."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112323",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-112323\nSeverity: high\nPackage: libgssapi-krb5-2\nVersion: 1.22.1-3\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-112323](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-112323)",
