            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-92389-curl",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-92389 high vulnerability for curl package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "libcurl's TFTP state machine fails to validate state transitions against the requested transfer direction, accepting opening server responses for both reads and writes interchangeably. A malicious TFTP server can respond to a download request in a way that forces the client into transmit mode, prompting libcurl to consume and transmit data from the handle's persistent `CURLOPT_READDATA` pointer - including data remaining from unrelated prior operations, such as an HTTP POST request executed on a reused handle."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92389",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-92389\nSeverity: high\nPackage: curl\nVersion: 8.22.0-1\nFix Version: 8.23.0~rc1-1\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-92389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92389)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-92389**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| high  | curl  | 8.22.0-1  | 8.23.0~rc1-1  | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-92389](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-92389)  |\n"
              },
