            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-85091-zlib1g",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-85091 high vulnerability for zlib1g package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "zlib versions 1.3.1.2 through 1.3.2 contain a heap buffer overflow vulnerability in the gz_vacate() function when processing non-blocking gzwrite() operations with stale external buffer pointers. Attackers can trigger the overflow by calling gzprintf() or gzvprintf() after a write stall, causing an unchecked memmove() to write beyond the internal input buffer boundary."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-85091",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-85091\nSeverity: high\nPackage: zlib1g\nVersion: 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.2-3\nFix Version: 1:1.3.dfsg+really1.3.2-4\nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-85091](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-85091)",
