            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-15534-perl-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-15534 medium vulnerability for perl-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "Perl versions through 5.45.1 have out-of-bounds heap reads and writes during regular expression matching via an undersized superlinear cache in S_regmatch.  The regex engine's superlinear cache holds one bit per subject position for each participating WHILEM node, so the bit count is the subject length plus one times the number of nodes. Nothing checks that product for positive overflow of the signed 32-bit count: a 286331153 byte subject matched against a pattern with 15 participating nodes stores the count as 14, leaving a two byte cache. The cache is then indexed from the real match position and node number, so reads go past the end of the allocation, and on failure CACHEsayNO sets a bit past it.  A caller that matches an attacker controlled subject of this size against a pattern of this shape can crash the process or corrupt heap memory."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534\nSeverity: medium\nPackage: perl-base\nVersion: 5.42.3-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-15534](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-15534**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| medium  | perl-base  | 5.42.3-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-15534](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-15534)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/perl-base@5.42.3-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=perl"
                ],
                "security-severity": "5.7"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-114690-gcc-16-base",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-114690 medium vulnerability for gcc-16-base package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in GCC. An out-of-bounds memory access vulnerability exists in the libstdc++ parallel search implementation due to an undersized internal buffer. A local attacker can exploit this flaw by providing crafted search data to an application compiled with parallel mode, causing the process to crash and leading to a Denial of Service (DoS)."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-114690",
