            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-53910-diffutils",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-53910 low vulnerability for diffutils package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "diff3 tool from GNU diffutils is vulnerable to a heap‑based buffer overflow due to multiple signed integer overflows in line‑mapping calculations. Incorrect arithmetic in mapping line ranges can result in corrupted values being used for memory allocation and loop bounds. When processing crafted diff output, these overflows may cause the application to allocate insufficient memory and subsequently perform out‑of‑bounds writes during internal processing.  An attacker who can control the output of the diff program used by diff3 (e.g. via --diff-program pointing to a malicious script) can trigger out-of-bounds writes, resulting in a crash and potentially remote code execution depending on the environment.   This issue has been fixed in commit 9ff04d5b84743e331e80b589335a52c5480d1815   NOTE: The project maintainers claim that this is not a security issue. They state that the worst outcome this issue can cause is a crash of diff and that it cannot be used to escalate privileges."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53910",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-53910\nSeverity: low\nPackage: diffutils\nVersion: 1:3.12-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-53910](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53910)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-53910**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | diffutils  | 1:3.12-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-53910](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-53910)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/diffutils@1%3A3.12-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "2.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56392-coreutils",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56392 low vulnerability for coreutils package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU coreutils unexpand is vulnerable to a heap-based buffer overflow due to an integer overflow during buffer allocation when processing large tab stop (-t) values. The multiplication used to calculate the allocation size can wrap around, resulting in an undersized buffer. When processing crafted input, subsequent writes exceed the allocated memory, leading to an out‑of‑bounds heap write.  When running GNU coreutils unexpand with attacker-provided large tab stop (-t) arguments, this behavior leads to a crash and potentially achieve a heap write primitive depending on memory layout.           This issue has been fixed in the commit b60a159fdc5bfcf9988d3a4cb6f53abe8ad5d35d"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-56392",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-56392\nSeverity: low\nPackage: coreutils\nVersion: 9.10-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-56392](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-56392)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-56392**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | coreutils  | 9.10-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-56392](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-56392)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/coreutils@9.10-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-22185-libldap2",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactIndirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-22185 low vulnerability for libldap2 package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "OpenLDAP Lightning Memory-Mapped Database (LMDB) versions 0.9.14 before 0.9.34, prior to commit 8e1fda8, contain a heap buffer underflow in the readline() function of mdb_load. When processing malformed input containing an embedded NUL byte, an unsigned offset calculation can underflow and cause an out-of-bounds read of one byte before the allocated heap buffer. This can cause mdb_load to crash, leading to a limited denial-of-service condition."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-22185",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-22185\nSeverity: low\nPackage: libldap2\nVersion: 2.6.14+dfsg-2\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-22185](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-22185)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-22185**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | libldap2  | 2.6.14+dfsg-2  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-22185](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-22185)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/libldap2@2.6.14%2Bdfsg-2?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian\u0026upstream=openldap"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.6"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56391-coreutils",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56391 low vulnerability for coreutils package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "GNU coreutils uniq is vulnerable to an out‑of‑bounds read due to incorrect handling of multibyte input when the -w (--check-chars) option is used. The find_field() function miscalculates the byte length of characters by repeatedly processing a fixed pointer instead of advancing through the input, resulting in an inflated length value.  This incorrect length is later used in a memcmp operation, causing reads beyond the allocated buffer when processing crafted multibyte input.  When running GNU coreutils uniq with attacker-provided arguments, this behavior leads to a crash and potential adjacent heap memory exposure.   This issue has been fixed in the commit d64e35a8a4c0e4608321433e0d84d917e4e36371."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-56391",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-56391\nSeverity: low\nPackage: coreutils\nVersion: 9.10-1\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-56391](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-56391)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-56391**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | coreutils  | 9.10-1  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-56391](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-56391)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/coreutils@9.10-1?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "6.1"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-102474-dash",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-102474 low vulnerability for dash package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in dash. The printf builtin reserves four bytes before converting a Unicode \\u or \\U escape, but the multi-byte token can need five or six bytes. A local user who can supply such an escape to dash printf or echo %b, including through dash -c and a positional argument, can write one or two bytes past that reservation."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-102474",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-102474\nSeverity: low\nPackage: dash\nVersion: 0.5.12-12\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-102474](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-102474)",
                "markdown": "**Vulnerability CVE-2026-102474**\n| Severity | Package | Version | Fix Version | Type | Location | Data Namespace | Link |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| low  | dash  | 0.5.12-12  |   | deb  | /var/lib/dpkg/status  | debian:distro:debian:unstable  | [CVE-2026-102474](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-102474)  |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "purls": [
                  "pkg:deb/debian/dash@0.5.12-12?arch=amd64\u0026distro=debian"
                ],
                "security-severity": "4.0"
              }
            },
            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-102473-dash",
              "name": "DpkgMatcherExactDirectMatch",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-102473 low vulnerability for dash package"
              },
              "fullDescription": {
                "text": "A flaw was found in dash. When built without libc fnmatch, the internal pmatch() matcher implements * by unbounded recursion over candidate positions. A local user who can plant filenames, or otherwise feed that matcher, can make a short multi-star pattern such as *.*.*.*.*.tar.gz consume excessive CPU."
              },
              "helpUri": "https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-102473",
              "help": {
                "text": "Vulnerability CVE-2026-102473\nSeverity: low\nPackage: dash\nVersion: 0.5.12-12\nFix Version: \nType: deb\nLocation: /var/lib/dpkg/status\nData Namespace: debian:distro:debian:unstable\nLink: [CVE-2026-102473](https://security-tracker.debian.org/tracker/CVE-2026-102473)",
